# State of the POC engine after the first real runs, read only.
# Date: 2026-11-21, after the apply of pull request 72. Context: us-east-1, account id and API id removed.

### P1 Worker function: state, engine and index key (environment names only)
$ aws lambda get-function-configuration --function-name mavenscout-engine-worker --query '{state,update,envNames,engine,indexKey}'
{
    "state": "Active",
    "update": "Successful",
    "runtime": "nodejs22.x",
    "memoryMb": 1024,
    "timeoutS": 180,
    "envNames": [
        "ENGINE_VARIANT",
        "JOBS_TABLE",
        "INDEX_ARTIFACT_S3_KEY",
        "ENGINE",
        "JOBS_BUCKET",
        "SUPABASE_SECRET_ID"
    ],
    "engine": "semantic",
    "indexKey": "index/index-13d7674312434864.json.gz",
    "supabaseSecretId": "mavenscout/supabase"
}
RESULT: ENGINE is semantic, the key points to index 13d7674312434864, the function is Active.

### P2 Api function: models given to every job (names and model ids only)
$ aws lambda get-function-configuration --function-name mavenscout-engine-api --query '{state,envNames,fit,text,embed}'
{
    "state": "Active",
    "update": "Successful",
    "envNames": [
        "ENGINE_VARIANT",
        "JOBS_TABLE",
        "EMBED_MODEL",
        "JOBS_QUEUE_URL",
        "JOBS_BUCKET",
        "TEXT_MODEL",
        "FIT_MODEL"
    ],
    "fit": "us.amazon.nova-lite-v1:0",
    "text": "us.amazon.nova-lite-v1:0",
    "embed": "amazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0"
}
RESULT: FIT_MODEL and TEXT_MODEL are the Nova Lite profile, EMBED_MODEL is Titan V2. ENGINE is not set on the api.

### P3 Bucket lifecycle rules
$ aws s3api get-bucket-lifecycle-configuration --bucket <jobs bucket> --query 'Rules[]'
[
    {
        "id": "abort-incomplete-uploads",
        "status": "Enabled",
        "prefix": "",
        "expireDays": null,
        "abortUploadsDays": 1
    },
    {
        "id": "expire-7-days-inputs",
        "status": "Enabled",
        "prefix": "inputs/",
        "expireDays": 7,
        "abortUploadsDays": null
    },
    {
        "id": "expire-7-days-results",
        "status": "Enabled",
        "prefix": "results/",
        "expireDays": 7,
        "abortUploadsDays": null
    }
]
RESULT: Only inputs/ and results/ expire after 7 days. A rule without a prefix aborts incomplete uploads after 1 day.

### P4 Index objects in the bucket
$ aws s3api list-objects-v2 --bucket <jobs bucket> --prefix index/ --query 'Contents[].[Key,Size]'
[
    [
        "index/index-13d7674312434864.json.gz",
        9442836
    ],
    [
        "index/index.json.gz",
        9442657
    ]
]
RESULT: Two objects: the first index and the current one, 9.4 MB gzipped each.

### P5 Dead letter queue depth
$ aws sqs get-queue-attributes --queue-url <dlq> --attribute-names ApproximateNumberOfMessages
{
    "Attributes": {
        "ApproximateNumberOfMessages": "0"
    }
}
RESULT: 0 messages.

### P6 Alarms of the engine that are not OK
$ aws cloudwatch describe-alarms --alarm-name-prefix mavenscout-engine --query "MetricAlarms[?StateValue!='OK']"
alarms in total: 17
[]
RESULT: No alarm outside OK.

### P7 Preflight from the origin of the local app
$ curl -i -X OPTIONS $API/jobs -H 'Origin: http://localhost:5173' -H 'Access-Control-Request-Method: POST' -H 'Access-Control-Request-Headers: content-type,idempotency-key'
HTTP/2 204 
access-control-allow-origin: http://localhost:5173
access-control-allow-methods: GET,POST
access-control-allow-headers: content-type,idempotency-key
access-control-max-age: 0
RESULT: 204, the origin http://localhost:5173 is allowed for GET and POST with the headers the app sends.
